Quartic graphs of girth six with eighteen hexagons through every edge
====================================================================

Claim: the minimum order is32 and exactly one graph attains it. This is
one lower-bound clause and one exact count from the fixed F012 source.
It is not a whole-source, conjecture, Lean or compression-factor claim.

Read eighteen.tex/pdf, source_contract.json and attribution.json. The new
outside-degree lemma makes every vertex visible at the first outside
boundary; no second-boundary assumption is needed. All canonical reuse
is verified by literal maps. The source witness map is checked separately.

Fresh complete verification:
  python check.py --study STUDY --out NEW_PRIVATE_DIRECTORY --render

The default rebuilds all programs and performs the complete228-matrix
root search and all bounded joins/completions, normally about four minutes.
Each command has a finite deadline. Reports fail on unfinished branches,
wrong input scope, changed bindings, malformed records or invalid maps.
Nauty64 supplies only map proposals; WORDSIZE64 and nauty_check are explicit.
Bounded controls were also run with address/undefined sanitizers; the full
large target enumeration has an ordinary complete execution, not a claimed
full sanitizer execution. Large historical root lists remain exact private
bindings rather than duplicate payloads; fresh replay reconstructs them.
